<title>USA: U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton consumption -- Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Census Bureau reports factory consumption of domestic and foreign cotton (bales):</p>
<p>    Jun 97-A   May 97-B    Jun 96   Cum 1997   Cum 1996</p>
<p>   1,030,327    840,092 1,040,258  5,346,937  5,220,525</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE CONSUMPTION OF ALL COTTON (bales):</p>
<p>    Jun 97-Y   May 97-X   Jun 96</p>
<p>	40,428     40,349   41,152</p>
<p>DAILY AVERAGE SPINDLE HOURS OPERATED:</p>
<p>    Jun 97-X   May 96-Y   Jun 96</p>
<p>	   142	  142	148</p>
<p>A-0 weeks. B-4 weeks. X-Based on 00 days. Y-20 days.</p>
</text>
